<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sikasso</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sikasso is a city in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a>, near the borders with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burkina-faso">Burkina Faso</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-coast">Côte d'Ivoire</a>. In the late 19th century it was the capital of the kingdom of Kenedougou, defended by a massive earthen wall that withstood <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samori-ture">Samori Ture</a>'s siege of 1887–1888. French forces stormed it in 1898.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sikasso.jpg" alt="Sikasso" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mousssa NIAKATE · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Le_grand_march%C3%A9_de_Sikasso.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
